"""STMicroelectronics STM32F412CEU6 - Arm Cortex-M4F MCU, UFQFPN48 (primitive).

Exact device: STM32F412CE, 512 KB flash, 256 KB SRAM, 100 MHz, UFQFPN48
7 x 7 mm, 0.5 mm pitch, 5.6 x 5.6 mm exposed pad (ST package code A0B9),
-40 to +85 C (suffix 6). Evidence: ST DS11139 Rev 9 - pinout Fig. 12 (p43),
pin definitions Table 9 (pp49-62), alternate functions Table 11 (pp66-71),
Fig. 12 labels pin 6 "PH0-OSC_OUT" (typo);
Table 9 name PH1-OSC_OUT is used. Package Fig. 63/64 + Table 101 (pp170-171), ordering Table 111 (p190).

Primitive package only: no decoupling, crystal, reset, or boot strap circuitry.
Integrator-owned support (DS11139):
- VDD (pins 24/36/48): one 100 nF per VDD/VSS pair plus one 4.7 uF ceramic on
  one VDD pin (Fig. 21 notes). 1.8-3.6 V: the 48-pin package has no PDR_ON pin,
  so the internal supervisor is always on (Sec. 3.18.1). The USB PHY supply
  (VDDUSB) is not bonded out; PA11/PA12 USB needs VDD >= 3.0 V (Table 16).
- VDDA/VREF+ (pin 9) with VSSA/VREF- (pin 8): 100 nF + 1 uF; VDDA must be at
  VDD potential (<= 300 mV difference during ramps) and VSSA = VSS (Table 16
  note 4, Fig. 21 note 4).
- VBAT (pin 1): 1.65-3.6 V backup domain; tie to VDD if no battery.
- VCAP_1 (pin 22): internal 1.2 V core regulator output. Single-VCAP package,
  so one 4.7 uF ceramic, ESR < 1 ohm, to VSS (p84 Table 18); the
  2 x 2.2 uF (ESR < 2 ohm) option applies only to 100/144-pin parts with VCAP_2. Not a supply rail -
  do not load or connect it to anything else.
- EP (pad 49): exposed die pad; ST recommends soldering it to PCB ground
  (Fig. 63 note 3). The land is plain copper with no thermal vias; the ST
  drawing does not require them.
- BOOT0 (pin 44) is a dedicated input (0-9 V, Table 16); PB2 is BOOT1.
- PC13-PC15 are on the backup power switch: <= 2 MHz, 30 pF, no sourcing
  (Table 9 note 2).
"""

VDD = io(Power(voltage="1.8V to 3.6V"))
VDDA = io(Power(voltage="1.8V to 3.6V"))
VBAT = io(Power(voltage="1.65V to 3.6V"))
VSS = io(Ground)
VSSA = io(Ground)
EP = io(Ground)
# Core-regulator decoupling node (V12 ~1.08-1.38 V); connect only the 4.7 uF cap.
VCAP = io(Net)

NRST = io(Net, optional=True)
BOOT0 = io(Net)
PA0 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA1 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA2 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA3 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA4 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA5 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA6 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA7 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA8 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA9 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA10 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA11 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA12 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA13 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA14 = io(Net, optional=True)
PA15 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB0 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB1 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB2 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB3 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB4 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB5 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB6 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB7 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB8 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB9 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB10 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB12 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB13 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB14 = io(Net, optional=True)
PB15 = io(Net, optional=True)
PC13 = io(Net, optional=True)
PC14_OSC32_IN = io(Net, optional=True)
PC15_OSC32_OUT = io(Net, optional=True)
PH0_OSC_IN = io(Net, optional=True)
PH1_OSC_OUT = io(Net, optional=True)

Component(
    name="STM32F412CEU6",
    symbol=Symbol(library="STM32F412CEU6.kicad_sym"),
    properties={
        # Ordering-only variant: identical die/package, tape-and-reel packing.
        "alternatives": [Part(mpn="STM32F412CEU6TR", manufacturer="STMicroelectronics")],
    },
    pins={
        "VBAT": VBAT,
        "VDD": VDD,
        "VDDA/VREF+": VDDA,
        "VSS": VSS,
        "VSSA/VREF-": VSSA,
        "EP": EP,
        "VCAP_1": VCAP,
        "NRST": NRST,
        "BOOT0": BOOT0,
        "PA0": PA0,
        "PA1": PA1,
        "PA2": PA2,
        "PA3": PA3,
        "PA4": PA4,
        "PA5": PA5,
        "PA6": PA6,
        "PA7": PA7,
        "PA8": PA8,
        "PA9": PA9,
        "PA10": PA10,
        "PA11": PA11,
        "PA12": PA12,
        "PA13": PA13,
        "PA14": PA14,
        "PA15": PA15,
        "PB0": PB0,
        "PB1": PB1,
        "PB2": PB2,
        "PB3": PB3,
        "PB4": PB4,
        "PB5": PB5,
        "PB6": PB6,
        "PB7": PB7,
        "PB8": PB8,
        "PB9": PB9,
        "PB10": PB10,
        "PB12": PB12,
        "PB13": PB13,
        "PB14": PB14,
        "PB15": PB15,
        "PC13": PC13,
        "PC14-OSC32_IN": PC14_OSC32_IN,
        "PC15-OSC32_OUT": PC15_OSC32_OUT,
        "PH0-OSC_IN": PH0_OSC_IN,
        "PH1-OSC_OUT": PH1_OSC_OUT,
    },
)
